# Brewfile entries an employer-managed Mac (DOTFILES_PROFILE=work in
# ~/.config/dotfiles/env) doesn't install. A separate file because
# script/update-brewfile regenerates the Brewfile with `brew bundle dump`,
# which would erase any conditionals written into it. See lib/profile.
# Format: <type> <name>, where type is brew, cask, mas or tap. For mas, `*`
# means every App Store app.

# Network filters: AdGuard's DNS proxy and content filter fight a corporate
# VPN or secure web gateway for the same traffic.
cask adguard

# Docker Desktop needs a paid subscription at larger companies; colima (with
# the docker CLI) from the Brewfile covers the same workflows.
cask docker-desktop

# Personal and consumer apps
cask google-drive
cask signal
cask steam

# A managed Mac may not allow signing in with a personal Apple ID, and a
# failed mas install stops brew bundle partway.
mas *
